{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nSlice C1 recorded below-seam ambient config/credential reads across the reconciler PASS CORE as `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows in `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py`; the in-process AST gate `check_config_ownership.py` still flags them. Sibling C3a-JIRA (a34b) owns the disjoint adapters/**+access_check.py surface — no conflict.\n\nThe 45 flagged reads (all flagged when drained; none already-owned): **`REBAR_ROOT` (12)** uniform `Path(os.environ.get(\"REBAR_ROOT\") or …parents[4])` and **`load_config` (17)** ambient `rebar.config.load_config()` (enumerated in clusters 1/2); **dynamic `os.environ.get` (7)** dead/toggle-only `_rebar_env`/`_env_int` bodies (`apply_handlers`,`apply_inbound`,`binding_store`,`inbound_translate`,`outbound_differ`×2,`rebar_id_audit`,`bridge_fsck_visibility`); **identity (3)** `REBAR_ENV_ID`(`inbound_translate`,`last_pass`×2)+`REBAR_AUTHOR`(`inbound_translate`); **tuning (2)** `RECONCILER_ABSENT_RETIRE_GRACE`(×2); **toggles (4)** see allowlist.\n\nAffected SOURCE: the modules above + `config.py` (resolvers) + `bridge_fsck.py` (L692 threads `env`) + `config_ownership_exceptions.py` (removes 45 rows). Affected TESTS (in-scope): `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` toggle + `test_identity_*` suites, `conftest.py`, binding tests setting `RECONCILER_ABSENT_RETIRE_GRACE`, `tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck.py` L166/L181 (pass explicit `env=`).\n\n## Outcome\nONE architectural cutover. The reconciler already composes ONE immutable `ReconcilerRuntime` per pass (`compose_reconciler_runtime` → `_operation_config.compose_operation_snapshot`, via `_PassContext` in `reconcile.reconcile_once`). This slice extends that seam to compose root + typed `Config` ONCE at pass entry — BEFORE the load/diff phase (`_load_snapshots`/`run_differs`) so every below-seam consumer has the value on `_PassContext` — replacing every below-seam ambient read; each gets one treatment and its `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` row removed. Portability: in-process AST gate (no CI-provider trigger). No stored-format change (pure routing; rollback = revert).\n\n## Decision rule\n- **(a) CUT-TO-SEAM (default; 41 reads).** A read whose value is composed config/root is resolved ONCE through an owned `config.py`/`_config_sources.py` resolver and THREADED into the below-seam helper; the ambient read no longer exists. Pass-stable values → compose-once-and-thread; LIVE per-operation reads stay owned-in-place (b) so a mid-operation override is never lost.\n- **(b) OWNED-IN-PLACE via `# read-via:` marker.** A read that is NOT composed config — a kill-switch, failure-injection toggle, or per-operation override — keeps a `# read-via:` marker naming the category. CAPPED at the 4 reads below = exactly **6 marked lines** (the gate flags each LINE); nothing else marked.\n\n### Owned-in-place allowlist (4 reads = 6 marked lines, the cap)\n1. `__main__.py L274` `REBAR_RECONCILER_LOCK_STEAL` — kill-switch (default ON; OFF = old exit-3). 1 line.\n2. `reconcile_helpers.py L629` `REBAR_RECONCILER_WRITE_FACADE` — AC6 rollback toggle. 1 line.\n3. `apply_handlers.py L184/424/462` `REBAR_RECONCILER_FAIL_SILENT_NOOP` — failure-injection test toggle, read live; inlined to a direct marked `os.environ.get` (the deleted `_rebar_env` wrapper clears the paired row). 3 lines.\n4. `apply_inbound.py L244` `REBAR_RECONCILER_CONFLICT_PARENT_ID` — per-conflict operator override (default `\"\"`), read live; inlined like (3). 1 line.\n\n## The cut, by cluster\n**Owned resolution (composition roots `config.py`/`_config_sources.py`):** REUSE the owned `rebar.config.repo_root` (=`_config_sources.repo_root`, explicit>`REBAR_ROOT`>git-top>cwd — the function `compose_operation_snapshot` already delegates to; no duplicate) and landed `compose_config()`. ADD `config.resolve_absent_retire_grace()` (raw env>default, clamp ≥1; no `cfg` param — a raw env knob, not a typed key). The three DISTINCT `REBAR_ENV_ID`/`REBAR_AUTHOR` reads are NOT unified — three owned accessors, one per call site, each verbatim (below).\n\n- **cluster 1 — `REBAR_ROOT` (12):** entrypoints (`__main__`,`reconcile`,`request`) call owned `rebar.config.repo_root()`; the composed root threads via `_PassContext.repo_root` to `applier`,`apply_inbound`,`apply_planning`,`dispatch_one`,`fetcher`,`inbound_translate`,`invariants`,`pass_io`,`_engine_support/reads`.\n- **cluster 2 — `load_config` (17):** the composed `Config` (+ runtime backend for the `select_backend` sites) threads into the 14 reconciler modules + `_engine_support/gates`,`lookups`,`reads` carrying the drained `load_config` rows; each reads its typed field (e.g. `sync.remote`, `deletion_probe_limit`).\n- **identity (3) — three per-call-site owned accessors, NOT unified, each verbatim:** (i) `last_pass.resolve_environment_id` L71: 3-tier `explicit>REBAR_ENV_ID(set-but-empty→error)>.env-id file→`local:`-prefix` — env read moves to an owned accessor, `last_pass` re-raises `LastPassError`; (ii) `last_pass` L329: None-able raw passthrough to `publish()` via owned `config.environment_id_or_none()` (no default/error); (iii) `inbound_translate` L174/175: default-when-UNSET via owned `config.reconciler_event_identity()`→`(env_id,author)`, `LEGACY_JIRA_*` defaults (empty→`''`, never raises), deleting the `_rebar_env` wrapper.\n- **tuning (2):** `config.resolve_absent_retire_grace()` threads into `binding_store`/`binding_walk` (deleting ambient `_env_int`/`_resolve_grace`).\n- **dead/rewired dynamic reads:** the `_rebar_env`/`_env_int` wrappers in `outbound_differ`, `rebar_id_audit` are unused → DELETED, clearing their `os.environ.get` rows (unmarked). `bridge_fsck_visibility` L73 (`src = os.environ if env is None else env`) is CUT by THIS change: drop the `env=None` default + `os.environ` branch → `src = env` (required). Serena inventory of callers-to-update: the SOLE production caller `bridge_fsck.py L692` (the `--live-visibility` CLI entrypoint / composition root) today passes NO `env` and relies on the fallback → updated to resolve and pass `env=`; the probe-only tests `test_bridge_fsck.py` L166/L181 (today `probe=` only) → pass explicit `env=` (L201 already does). Both are in the inventory below.\n- Remove the 45 rows.\n**Shared-helper re-derivation (Serena `find_referencing_symbols`):** `_engine_support/reads.py`,`lookups.py`,`gates.py` have CLI/MCP callers outside the pass → signatures UNCHANGED, the ambient read becomes INTERNAL delegation to the owned resolver; pass-internal call sites RECEIVE the threaded value.\n\n## Testing (RED → GREEN)\nHeld-out `tests/scripts/test_reconciler_core_seam_clean_heldout.py` (`import check_config_ownership`) asserts: (i) `check(REPO_ROOT)` has no finding for any listed path; (ii) `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` has zero entries for a listed file; (iii) `# read-via:` markers total exactly **6** — `__main__.py`(1),`reconcile_helpers.py`(1),`apply_handlers.py`(3),`apply_inbound.py`(1), else 0. RED now. New-boundary asserts: grace `<1`→1 and unset→default; set-but-empty `REBAR_ENV_ID`→`LastPassError` vs `inbound_translate` empty→`''`; `FAIL_SILENT_NOOP`/`CONFLICT_PARENT_ID` set mid-operation still observed live. Regression green: `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/**`, the reconciler `tests/interfaces`/`integration` paths, and the consumers above.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No ambient config/credential read remains below the seam: each is cut-to-seam (41) or one of the 4 owned-in-place reads (6 marked lines); nothing else marked.\n- [ ] The 45 `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows are removed and `check_config_ownership.py` passes with no path-glob exception (held-out marker-total==6 / per-file check).\n- [ ] Root + typed `Config` are composed ONCE at pass entry (before the load/diff phase) and threaded via `_PassContext`; the three identity reads keep distinct per-call-site semantics; shared `_engine_support` helpers + `bridge_fsck.py` L692 resolve/thread from the composition root (signatures unchanged).\n- [ ] Regression suites in Testing pass; provider-neutral outcomes unchanged."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787110081927783001,"uuid":"9208fce7-241b-4fcc-ad50-bad9dfa740ed"}